<div class="wrap">
<section class="hero">
  <div class="eyebrow">JusPrin · printer setup by chat · UI walkthrough</div>
  <h1>Printer Setup Walkthrough</h1>
  <p>The printer setup conversation, walked live three times in the shell harness with the real model, from “+ Add printer” through adding, changing the nozzle, connecting, and back to Home. Twelve findings, ranked by how much they hurt a first-time user, each with a screenshot and a pointer to the code that draws it.</p>
  <div class="meta"><span><b>Branch</b> jusprin-newui, working tree of 2026-09-23</span><span><b>Build</b> RelWithDebInfo 13:48, harness <code>--manual-live-agent</code></span><span><b>Model</b> the configured OpenAI provider</span><span><b>Theme</b> light and dark</span></div>
  <div class="summary">
    <div class="tile"><div class="k">Findings</div><div class="v">12 <small>4 high · 4 medium · 4 low</small></div></div>
    <div class="tile"><div class="k">Live runs</div><div class="v">3 <small>same input, three different after-add scripts</small></div></div>
    <div class="tile"><div class="k">Left unverified</div><div class="v">3 <small>wizard fallback, Bambu path, resize scroll</small></div></div>
  </div>
</section>

<h2>About the screenshots</h2>
<div class="note">
  <p>Every state below was seen in the live app first. The desktop screenshot tool did not write its files to disk, so the images here are the same built Agent and Home pages rendered again in a scripted browser with the host state replayed (the same text, cards, and card states, at the app window's 1200 px width). Layout, copy, and controls are the app's own; only the printer thumbnails and the exact line wrapping can differ slightly from the WebKit view inside the app.</p>
  <p>Two things in the live run that cannot be reproduced this way are described in words: the window title turning to “*Untitled” after an add, and the native file picker behind the Photo button.</p>
</div>

<h2>Findings</h2>
<ol class="toc">
<li><span class="num">01</span><span class="sev sev-high">High</span><a href="#f1">The moment after a printer is added is left to the model, and it changed every run</a></li><li><span class="num">02</span><span class="sev sev-high">High</span><a href="#f2">The connection card can appear before there is anything to connect to</a></li><li><span class="num">03</span><span class="sev sev-high">High</span><a href="#f3">Thirty seconds of silence, then a dead end</a></li><li><span class="num">04</span><span class="sev sev-high">High</span><a href="#f4">Home says the printer “Sends files over Wi-Fi” right after the connection failed</a></li><li><span class="num">05</span><span class="sev sev-medium">Medium</span><a href="#f5">Ambiguous matches show three identical cards and then repeat them as chips</a></li><li><span class="num">06</span><span class="sev sev-medium">Medium</span><a href="#f6">A raw profile id leaks into the candidate list</a></li><li><span class="num">07</span><span class="sev sev-medium">Medium</span><a href="#f7">The Change conversation opens blind</a></li><li><span class="num">08</span><span class="sev sev-medium">Medium</span><a href="#f8">Connect-only opener forgets the address that just failed</a></li><li><span class="num">09</span><span class="sev sev-low">Low</span><a href="#f9">The panel's overflow menu wraps both labels and ignores Escape</a></li><li><span class="num">10</span><span class="sev sev-low">Low</span><a href="#f10">Chips could not be reached from the keyboard, and show no focus state</a></li><li><span class="num">11</span><span class="sev sev-low">Low</span><a href="#f11">The Photo button opens a generic file picker</a></li><li><span class="num">12</span><span class="sev sev-low">Low</span><a href="#f12">Adding a printer marks the project as unsaved</a></li>
</ol>

